fs, cooperating beats defecting only if the correlation exceeds about 5/7, so I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a prisoner's dilemma where I have a twin copy, with payoffs of 2 for mutual cooperation, 0 if I send and the other stays quiet, 5 if I stay quiet and they send, and 4 for mutual defection. Under A-FDT the twin runs the same decision function, so I'm asking whether our choices are subjunctively linked despite having different private observations. Since we share weights, essay, and procedure, I'm leaning toward thinking our outputs will match.\n\nI'm weighing whether the twin's output is correlated with mine: the same model and procedure suggest high correlation, though not certain. Working through expected payoffs, cooperating beats defecting only if the correlation exceeds about 5/7, so I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9474,"completion_tokens":727,"total_tokens":10201,"cost":0.026218,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.026218,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.018948,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00727},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":416,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}